course: dictionary
lesson: 2370
title: Culture and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Culture is a word with more than one meaning, so context matters. Its main meaning is the way of life of a group of people: their language, food, clothes, beliefs, customs, festivals, music and art. «Chopsticks are never stuck upright in rice, because in some Asian cultures that looks like a funeral custom.» The clue is custom: culture here means the habits and beliefs a group shares.
explain: Read the words around the word for more clues. «Almost every culture remembers its dead, gathers people together, often shares food, and shows love and respect in its own way.» Every group has its own culture, so a culture is the particular way one group does these things. The sentence never says one way is right, only that each group has its own way.
explain: Culture can also mean art, music, books and theatre all together, or the habits shared by a group such as a school or team, as in a culture of kindness. Try each meaning in the sentence. If your meaning still makes sense, you have probably found the right one.
fact: Culture means the way of life of a group of people, including their language, food, customs and beliefs.
fact: «Cultural» is the adjective: it describes something to do with a culture, such as a cultural festival.
fact: «Multicultural» means containing many different cultures, as in a multicultural city.
fact: Culture can also mean art, music and books together, or the ideas and habits shared by a group, like a culture of kindness.
fact: In science, a culture is tiny living things, such as bacteria, grown on purpose in a dish for study.
exercise: «Chopsticks are never stuck upright in rice, because in some Asian cultures that looks like a funeral custom.» In this sentence, what does culture mean? | Tiny living things grown in a dish | A kind of sticky rice | *The way of life and customs of a group of people | A sport played at school
exercise: Lily says culture is only about art. What is the best answer? | No, culture means a dish of food | Yes, but only in science lessons | Yes, culture is only art and music | *No, culture also means the way of life of a group of people
exercise: In science, what can a culture be? | A group of friends who play together | A painting in a gallery | *Tiny living things, like bacteria, grown in a dish | A type of rice
test: «Mo's class has a culture of kindness, so everyone helps.» What does culture mean here? | A school trip | Tiny living things grown in a dish | Art and music only | *The ideas and habits shared by a group
test: Which word is the adjective that describes something to do with a culture? | Cult | Culturals | Culturing | *Cultural
exam: «Popular culture» means what? | *Art, music and other creative activities enjoyed by many people | A group of peasants who farm the land | Bacteria grown in a dish | Cooking rice in a funny way
